From e0db43a08ca3472b10b57167b45f0b0fdfad3f30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy <andylee77@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:09:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/22] thingino-raptor: streaming and encoder rate-control,
 Image Quality, motion gating

raptor patches 0109-0111: JPEG rings sized for the largest JPEG, S31raptor
exports /etc/default/raptor to the daemons, and rvd reports which ISP
controls the HAL has (get-isp-caps).

The Streamer pages apply a stream as one change from per-camera menus;
Image Quality shows only the controls the HAL applies, its noise-reduction
knobs on the agent's noise_reduction and temporal_noise_reduction; there are
no on-camera motion controls where the HAL has no IVS
(raptor-sigmastar.webui.json, S32raptor-motion, raptor-motion-watch). The
agent adapter carries the server side of these and of the Ch1 preview
fallback: the stream state with its video-memory cost, the ISP caps, motion.
